sn11.17:2.1 starts: “Rise up, O hero, victor in battle!
sn11.17:2.2 starts: Your burden lowered, debt-free one, wander in the
sn11.17:4.1 starts: “Rise up, O hero, victor in battle!
sn11.17:4.2 starts: O caravan leader, debt-free one, wander in the
sn11.18:3.1 starts: Sakka:
sn11.18:3.2 starts: Those versed in the Triple Veda,
sn11.18:3.3 starts: All the khattiyas reigning on earth,
sn11.18:3.4 starts: The Four Great Kings and the glorious Thirty—
sn11.18:7.1 starts: The Blessed One:
sn11.18:7.2 starts: Having worshipped the different quarters,
sn11.18:7.3 starts: The deva-king Maghava, Suja’s husband,
sn11.18:7.4 starts: The chief, climbed into his chariot.”
sn11.19:3.1 starts: Sakka:
sn11.19:3.2 starts: In this world with its devas,
sn11.19:3.3 starts: The Teacher of perfect name:
sn11.19:3.4 starts: He is the one whom I worship, Matali.
sn11.19:6.1 starts: Matali:
sn11.19:6.2 starts: Are indeed the best in the world.
sn11.19:7.1 starts: The Blessed One:
sn11.19:7.2 starts: Having worshipped the Blessed One,
sn11.19:7.3 starts: The deva-king Maghava, Suja’s husband,
sn11.19:7.4 starts: The chief, climbed into his chariot.”
sn11.1:5.2 starts: Might achieve unending bliss:
sn11.1:5.3 starts: Go there, Suvīra,
sn11.1:6.1 starts: Suvīra:
sn11.1:6.2 starts: Without doing work, O Sakka,
sn11.20:8.1 starts: Matali:
sn11.20:8.2 starts: Are indeed the best in the world.
sn11.20:9.1 starts: The Blessed One:
sn11.20:9.2 starts: Having worshipped the Bhikkhu Saṅgha,
sn11.20:9.3 starts: The deva-king Maghava, Suja’s husband,
sn11.20:9.4 starts: The chief, climbed into his chariot.”
